\hypertarget{glossary}{%
\section{Glossary}\label{glossary}}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 2\tabcolsep) * \real{0.1189}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 2\tabcolsep) * \real{0.8811}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Accronym}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Significance}
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\textbf{FL} & Federated Learning trains models across distributed
clinics without centralizing raw data, enabling HeartLine's
privacy-preserving diagnostics for secure collaboration in Algeria. \\
\textbf{ECG} & Electrocardiogram records heart electrical activity,
serving as HeartLine's core data for AI-driven arrhythmia detection to
address Algeria's CVD burden. \\
\textbf{GNN} & Graph Neural Networks process ECG lead relationships as
graphs, enhancing HeartLine's detection of rare arrhythmias with high
accuracy. \\
\textbf{CNN} & Convolutional Neural Networks extract temporal features
from ECGs, powering HeartLine's efficient arrhythmia diagnostics. \\
\textbf{DP} & Differential Privacy adds noise to model updates, ensuring
patient data confidentiality in HeartLine's FL framework, a key market
advantage. \\
\textbf{CVD} & Cardiovascular Diseases, causing 30\% of deaths in
Algeria, drive HeartLine's mission for accessible AI diagnostics. \\
\textbf{1D-CNN} & 1D Convolutional Neural Networks process ECG
time-series data, delivering high-accuracy arrhythmia detection in
HeartLine's pipeline. \\
\textbf{ResNet-50} & A 50-layer residual network with skip connections
captures complex ECG patterns, improving HeartLine's diagnostic
precision. \\
\textbf{GAN} & Generative Adversarial Networks generate synthetic ECGs,
addressing data scarcity in HeartLine's training for robust models. \\
\textbf{DA} & Data Augmentation introduces variations (e.g., scaling,
noise) to ECGs, enhancing HeartLine's model robustness for diverse
datasets in Algeria. \\
\textbf{QRS} & QRS Detection identifies ventricular depolarization in
ECGs, a critical preprocessing step for HeartLine's accurate feature
extraction. \\
\textbf{F1} & F1-score balances precision and recall, measuring
HeartLine's diagnostic accuracy (\textgreater0.90) for arrhythmias in
benchmarks. \\
\textbf{AUC} & Area Under the Curve evaluates HeartLine's ability to
distinguish ECG classes (\textgreater0.90), validating its diagnostic
power. \\
\textbf{HE} & Homomorphic Encryption allows secure computations on
encrypted data, enhancing HeartLine's FL security. \\
\textbf{SA} & Secure Aggregation encrypts model updates, ensuring
privacy during HeartLine's FL training. \\
\textbf{TM} & Telemedicine enables remote ECG analysis, supporting
HeartLine's deployment in underserved Algerian regions. \\
\textbf{HL7} & Health Level Seven standard facilitates HeartLine's
integration with EHR systems, ensuring interoperability. \\
\textbf{FHIR} & Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources standard
supports HeartLine's seamless data exchange with healthcare systems. \\
\textbf{BWR} & Baseline Wander Removal eliminates low-frequency ECG
noise, improving data quality for HeartLine's AI models. \\
\textbf{NR} & Noise Reduction removes ECG artifacts, ensuring clean data
for HeartLine's accurate diagnostics. \\
\textbf{PESTEL} & Political, Economic, Social, Technological,
Environmental, and Legal analysis assesses external factors for
HeartLine's market strategy, guiding its positioning in Algeria. \\
\textbf{SWOT} & Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats
analysis evaluates HeartLine's strategic positioning, highlighting
competitive advantages like privacy. \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

\hypertarget{general-introduction}{%
\section{General Introduction}\label{general-introduction}}

\textbf{i. Context and Motivation}

At Ibn Rochd Hospital in Annaba, 55-year-old Fatima clutched an ECG
strip in her trembling hands, breathless and in pain. The only on-site
cardiologist, overwhelmed with a backlog of critical cases, failed to
promptly detect a life-threatening arrhythmia. Hours passed before
proper intervention, underscoring a healthcare reality that is both
personal and systemic.

Cardiovascular diseases (CVDs) account for nearly 30\% of total
mortality in Algeria {[} {]}, with diagnostic disparities particularly
acute in rural and underserved regions. Manual ECG interpretation
remains prone to delays and errors, compounded by a shortage of
specialists. In this context, digital transformation in cardiac
diagnostics is not just desirable --- it is essential.

This alarming gap in healthcare equity inspired the creation of
\textbf{HeartLine}: an AI-powered platform designed to deliver accurate,
real-time, and privacy-preserving cardiac diagnosis. Developed at the
\textbf{University of Badji Mokhtar -- Annaba}, HeartLine represents a
fusion of \textbf{Artificial Intelligence (AI)}, \textbf{Federated
Learning (FL)}, and \textbf{Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)}. The system is
envisioned not only as a clinical tool, but as a strategic response to
Algeria's pressing health innovation needs.

\textbf{ii. Problem Statement}

Manual ECG interpretation in Algeria faces systemic inefficiencies:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  Diagnostic delays due to overwhelmed personnel
\item
  Error rates exceeding 15\%
\item
  Lack of specialists in non-urban and rural regions
\item
  Limited adoption of Computer-Aided Diagnosis (CAD) tools due to poor
  interoperability and weak privacy safeguards
\end{itemize}

These constraints result in delayed or missed detection of
life-threatening arrhythmias. While some CAD solutions exist, most lack
the adaptability, privacy compliance, and real-world applicability
needed in the Algerian context.

\textbf{HeartLine aims to address these challenges by:}

\begin{itemize}
\item
  Automating arrhythmia detection with an accuracy target of over 95\%
\item
  Preserving patient data privacy via Federated Learning
\item
  Seamlessly integrating with hospital systems through HL7 and FHIR
  standards
\item
  Adapting to rural and urban settings alike, even under bandwidth and
  hardware constraints
\end{itemize}

\textbf{iii. Research Questions}

To evaluate the feasibility and performance of HeartLine, the following
research questions are formulated:

\begin{enumerate}
\def\labelenumi{\arabic{enumi}.}
\item
  \textbf{How do preprocessing and data augmentation techniques affect
  ECG classification accuracy in AI systems?}
\item
  \textbf{Can federated learning effectively preserve patient privacy
  while maintaining high diagnostic accuracy?}
\item
  \textbf{Which classifiers (MLP, KNN, RF, SVM, XGBoost) perform best
  within a federated GNN-based cardiac diagnosis system?}
\item
  \textbf{How can AI-based CAD systems bridge diagnostic disparities in
  rural Algerian healthcare environments?}
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{iv. Hypothesis}

This research is based on the central hypothesis that:

\textbf{A federated GNN model, enhanced with domain-specific ECG
augmentation techniques and deployed securely at the edge, will achieve
diagnostic accuracy greater than 95\%, while preserving patient data
privacy and supporting deployment in resource-constrained Algerian
healthcare settings.}

\textbf{v. Research Method Summary}

This project follows a hybrid methodology combining:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Quantitative experimentation}: development of a GNN-based ECG
  classification model, enhanced through augmentation strategies and
  trained using federated learning paradigms.
\item
  \textbf{Federated simulation}: validation of the system's performance
  across decentralized data nodes, simulating multiple hospitals without
  centralizing patient data.
\item
  \textbf{Comparative classifier benchmarking}: testing performance of
  MLP, KNN, RF, SVM, and XGBoost models in both centralized and
  federated contexts.
\item
  \textbf{Technical prototype development}: full-stack implementation of
  the HeartLine SaaS platform, including preprocessing pipeline, model
  integration, and edge deployment.
\item
  \textbf{Commercial viability analysis}: incorporating strategic tools
  (SWOT, 7P, PESTEL, BMC) and financial planning to evaluate the
  startup\textquotesingle s sustainability.
\item
  \textbf{Regulatory and ethical alignment}: ensuring compliance with
  Algerian Decree No. 22-187 (Sept 27, 2022), and with international
  standards on data privacy (GDPR-inspired FL compliance).
\end{itemize}

\textbf{vi. Structure of the Dissertation}

This dissertation is organized into \textbf{five chapters}, each
corresponding to a foundational axis of the HeartLine diagnostic AI
project:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Chapter 1 -- Scientific Foundations and Problem Context\\
  }Introduces the burden of cardiovascular disease globally and in
  Algeria, outlines conventional ECG diagnostics, and surveys relevant
  AI techniques. It also defines the research hypothesis and ethical
  positioning of the study.
\item
  \textbf{Chapter 2 -- Data Strategy, Methodology, and Evaluation
  Metrics\\
  }Details the dataset curation process, benchmarking approach, and
  multi-phase methodology underpinning HeartLine. It outlines how
  reproducibility, fairness, and clinical relevance are ensured through
  metrics like AUC, F1-score, and inference latency.
\item
  \textbf{Chapter 3 -- System Architecture and Innovation Logic\\
  }Describes the technical design of HeartLine, including lightweight
  deep learning architectures, federated learning protocols, edge
  optimization strategies, and security mechanisms (e.g., DP, HE). It
  also contextualizes these innovations within Algeria's healthcare
  infrastructure.
\item
  \textbf{Chapter 4 -- Strategic Positioning and Market Analysis\\
  }Explores HeartLine's commercial and deployment strategy through SWOT
  analysis, competitor benchmarking, the 7Ps framework, and PESTEL
  factors. The Business Model is introduced to map HeartLine's viability
  within emerging diagnostic ecosystems.
\item
  \textbf{Chapter 5 -- Prototype Development and Strategic
  Deliverables\\
  }Presents the system execution roadmap, including team structure,
  timeline, and technical fiche. It outlines the iterative development
  phases, validation protocol, pilot simulation environment, and
  concludes with policy recommendations and deployment pathways.
\end{itemize}

The \textbf{General Conclusion} revisits the central hypothesis,
synthesizes key findings from all chapters, assesses the societal and
clinical impact of the HeartLine system, and identifies future research
and development opportunities.

\hypertarget{part-1-foundations-and-system-design}{%
\subsubsection{Part 1: Foundations and System
Design}\label{part-1-foundations-and-system-design}}

\hypertarget{chapter-1-scientific-and-theoretical-foundations}{%
\section{Chapter 1: Scientific and Theoretical
Foundations}\label{chapter-1-scientific-and-theoretical-foundations}}

\hypertarget{first-chapter-introduction}{%
\subsection{\texorpdfstring{ First Chapter
Introduction}{ First Chapter Introduction}}\label{first-chapter-introduction}}

Cardiovascular diseases (CVDs) remain the leading cause of death
worldwide, claiming 17.9 million lives each year. In Algeria, they are
responsible for 30\% of total mortality---well above the global
average---posing a critical public health challenge (World Health
Organization, 2024; Algerian Ministry of Health, 2023). This crisis is
particularly severe in rural areas, where healthcare infrastructure is
limited and cardiology expertise is scarce, resulting in frequent delays
in diagnosis and treatment.

In Tamanrasset, one of Algeria's most remote southern provinces, clinics
in regions like Idlès and Abalessa often lack cardiologists and rely on
basic ECG equipment. At the Tamanrasset District Polyclinic, ECGs are
performed by general practitioners, but interpretation depends on
transferring the results to specialists in distant cities such as
Ouargla or Algiers. With transportation, communication, and
administrative bottlenecks, this process can take over 24 hours---time
during which cardiac conditions may deteriorate.

HeartLine offers a practical and scalable solution by introducing a
privacy-preserving, AI-powered ECG diagnostic system. Built on Federated
Learning (FL) and optimized Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs), the
system enables accurate, real-time cardiac analysis directly at the
point of care---without compromising patient data privacy. By equipping
rural clinics with on-site AI tools, HeartLine reduces critical delays,
supports faster triage, and helps close the urban-rural healthcare gap.
It also lays the groundwork for broader deployment of ethical,
data-secure AI in low-resource health systems globally.

\hypertarget{medical-and-scientific-context}{%
\subsection{1.1 Medical and Scientific
Context}\label{medical-and-scientific-context}}

This section outlines the scientific and theoretical basis for the
HeartLine project, covering cardiology, AI, and privacy technologies.

\hypertarget{cardiovascular-disease-burden-and-diagnostic-challenges-in-algeria}{%
\subsubsection{1.1.1 Cardiovascular Disease Burden and Diagnostic
Challenges in
Algeria}\label{cardiovascular-disease-burden-and-diagnostic-challenges-in-algeria}}

This subsection addresses the epidemiological landscape of
cardiovascular diseases (CVDs) in Algeria, where CVDs account for over
36\% of deaths. Key modifiable risk factors such as hypertension (35\%),
diabetes (15\%), and smoking are widespread. Diagnostic delays averaging
12 hours in rural areas are exacerbated by shortages of cardiologists
and fragmented infrastructure
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}1{]}}}.

