Atrial Fibrillation (AF) & 2.5\% (adults \textgreater{} 60) & Aligns
with global trends but poses high stroke risk if
undiagnosed/mismanaged. \\
Heart Failure (HF) & 1.8\% (national adult population) & Projected to
rise with aging demographics and increasing risk factors. \\
Hypertension & 35\% & Often poorly controlled due to lack of awareness,
adherence, and monitoring access. \\
Diabetes Mellitus & 15\% & Accelerates atherosclerosis, increases
cardiac complication risk. \\
Dyslipidemia & High prevalence & Linked to dietary habits and lack of
preventive screening. \\
Obesity/Inactivity & Significant contributor & Lifestyle factors driving
metabolic syndrome and increased cardiovascular strain. \\
Smoking & Significant contributor & Major risk factor for vascular
damage and Coronary Artery Disease (CAD). \\
Diagnostic Delay (rural) & 12 hours (average) & Attributable to
cardiologist shortage and fragmented infrastructure, turning treatable
conditions into emergencies. \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

\textbf{Source :} Khosravi et al. (2024), based on GBD 1990--2021 data.

This table provides a concise overview of the specific epidemiological
burden. The high prevalence of modifiable risk factors like hypertension
and diabetes indicates that targeted public health interventions
alongside technological solutions like HeartLine are crucial. The
striking 12-hour average diagnostic delay in rural areas directly
validates HeartLine\textquotesingle s mission to improve access and
speed diagnosis.

Socioeconomic barriers like low health literacy, cultural factors, and
transportation costs exacerbate these issues, hindering timely medical
attention.

