with Applications, 224}, 120107.
\url{https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eswa.2023.120107}.

This figure illustrates the transformation of 12-lead ECG data into a
graph format suitable for Graph Neural Networks (GNNs). Each lead is
represented as a node, while edges reflect anatomical or functional
relationships between leads (e.g., II--III--aVF for inferior wall;
V1--V6 for precordial groupings). This visual structure offers an
intuitive understanding of how spatial and temporal ECG features can be
modeled as a graph for advanced AI-based interpretation
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}8{]}}}.

