and fully connected layers to the final output. It emphasizes the
sequential processing of temporal features critical for ECG
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}14{]}}}.

\textbf{b) Residual Networks (ResNet-50 Adaptation)}

To tackle complex arrhythmia detection, HeartLine employs a 1D-adapted
ResNet-50. Skip connections in ResNet allow the training of deep models
without gradient loss, enabling superior accuracy (\textgreater90\%
F1-score) for nuanced cardiac events like bundle branch blocks and
infarctions.

The neural network architecture for HeartLine is shown in \textbf{Figure
A.9 (Appendix A)}.

This diagram details the structure of HeartLine's convolutional and
graph neural networks, optimized for ECG analysis. Its high performance
(F1-score \textgreater0.90, section 1.3.2) enables detection of complex
and rare arrhythmias, strengthening HeartLine's competitive edge over
platforms like Qardiax (section 3.2).

\textbf{c) Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) for Lead Dependency Modeling}

HeartLine models 12-lead ECG signals as a graph structure, with each
lead as a node and edges denoting spatial or functional dependencies.
GNNs capture subtle inter-lead patterns crucial for diagnosing rare or
spatially diffuse arrhythmias.

\textbf{\emph{Mathematical Formulation of Graph Convolutional Layers:}
\protect\hyperlink{references}{{[}15{]}}}

A foundational GNN layer, the Graph Convolutional Network (GCN) layer,
aggregates information from node neighbors:

H(l+1)=sigma(tildeD−frac12tildeAtildeD−frac12H(l)W(l)). Where:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  H(l) is the matrix of node features at layer l. For ECG, H(0) is the
  time-series signal for each lead.
\item
  tildeA=A+I\_N is the adjacency matrix with added self-loops.
\item
  tildeD is the diagonal degree matrix of tildeA, used for
  normalization.
\item
  W(l) is the learnable weight matrix for layer l.
\item
  sigma(cdot) is a non-linear activation function (e.g., ReLU).
\end{itemize}

This mathematical formulation explains how GNNs effectively perform a
weighted average of neighbor features, enabling the network to learn
spatially informed representations. For HeartLine, GNNs are crucial for
identifying subtle, spatially distributed patterns in rare arrhythmias,
improving recall by \textbf{10\%} for these conditions.

\textbf{d) Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) for Data Augmentation}

GANs help address class imbalance by generating high-fidelity synthetic
ECGs. HeartLine uses a clinically validated GAN pipeline where expert
cardiologists review generated data to ensure realism and diagnostic
utility \protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}16{]}}}.

\textbf{Table 09: HeartLine\textquotesingle s Clinician Evaluation
Protocol for Synthetic ECG Data}

