\textbf{1. Blind Review Panels} & Cardiologists review mixed
real/synthetic ECGs without knowing origin. & Eliminates bias, ensures
unbiased assessment of realism. \\
\textbf{2. Diagnostic Accuracy Assessment} & Clinicians diagnose and
rate quality/plausibility (Likert scale 1-5). & Quantifies clinical
utility and physiological fidelity of synthetic data. \\
\textbf{3. Statistical Comparison} & Compare diagnoses/ratings of
synthetic vs. real ECGs. & Validates synthesis success if high
concordance is observed. \\
\textbf{4. Feature-Specific Validation} & Assess fidelity of critical
ECG features (P-wave, QRS, ST-segment). & Ensures synthetic data
contains diagnostically relevant information. \\
\textbf{5. Iterative Feedback} & Insights guide GAN training refinements
(architecture, loss functions). & Continuously improves realism and
clinical value of synthetic data. \\
