\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\textbf{Time-Domain Features} & \textbf{RR Interval:} Time between
R-peaks (heart rate, rhythm).

\textbf{HRV (SDNN, RMSSD, pNN50):} Autonomic nervous system activity.

\textbf{PR Interval:} Atrioventricular conduction.

\textbf{QRS Duration:} Ventricular depolarization time.

\textbf{QT Interval:} Ventricular depolarization/repolarization.

\textbf{ST Segment Elevation/Depression:} Myocardial
ischemia/infarction.

\textbf{T-wave Morphology:} Ischemia, electrolyte imbalances. &
Fundamental for rhythm analysis, detecting conduction abnormalities, and
identifying ischemic changes. \\
\textbf{Frequency-Domain Features} & \textbf{Power Spectral Density
(PSD) from FFT:} Distribution of power across frequencies (rhythm
irregularities).

\textbf{Frequency Bins (VLF, LF, HF):} For detailed HRV analysis.

\textbf{Wavelet Transform Coefficients:} Time-frequency analysis,
denoising, feature extraction at different scales. & Provide insights
into underlying cardiac electrical activity, useful for complex
arrhythmias and subtle signal components. \\
\textbf{Morphological Features} & \textbf{QRS Complex Morphology:}
Notches, slurring, width (bundle branch blocks, hypertrophy).

\textbf{P-wave Morphology:} Atrial abnormalities.

\textbf{T-wave Inversion/Flattening:} Ischemia, electrolyte imbalances.
& Capture specific shapes and patterns critical for differentiating
various cardiac conditions and abnormalities. \\
