\hypertarget{project-methodology}{%
\subsubsection{1.3.3 Project Methodology}\label{project-methodology}}

\textbf{a) Development Lifecycle}

The HeartLine project follows a rigorous, multi-stage methodology to
ensure the development of a high-performing, ethical, and deployable AI
diagnostic system.

The ECG data flow and patient journey are provided in \textbf{Figure A.5
(Appendix A)}.

This diagram maps the journey of ECG data from patient acquisition
through preprocessing, training, and inference, integrating technical
and patient-centric perspectives. It supports the technical feasibility
validated in section 1.3.2 and addresses Algeria's cardiovascular
disease burden (section 3.1.3).

The next table provides a concise, structured overview of
HeartLine\textquotesingle s development lifecycle. Each phase builds
upon the previous one, ensuring a systematic and thorough approach from
data handling to model deployment. This outlines the logical progression
of the project.

\textbf{Table 18: HeartLine Project Methodology Overview}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.2379}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3935}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3686}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Phase}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Key Activities}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Expected Outcomes}
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\textbf{1. Data Acquisition \& Curation} & Collect diverse public/local
ECG datasets, ethical review, initial annotation. & Diverse,
high-quality, ethically approved ECG datasets. \\
\textbf{2. Data Preprocessing \& Augmentation} & Denoising,
segmentation, normalization, GAN-based synthesis, geometric
augmentation. & Clean, standardized, augmented ECG datasets, addressing
noise and class imbalance. \\
\textbf{3. Expert Feature Extraction} & Compute time-domain,
frequency-domain, and morphological features; PCA/t-SNE. & Rich,
interpretable feature vectors from ECG signals. \\
\textbf{4. Model Training (Federated Learning)} & Initialize global
model, local training, DP, HE, secure aggregation (FedAvg). & Robust,
privacy-preserving global AI model for cardiac diagnosis. \\
\textbf{5. Model Evaluation \& Validation} & Performance metrics (AUC,
F1), fairness assessment, clinician validation. & Validated AI models
with high accuracy and equitable performance. \\
\textbf{6. Edge Model Optimization} & Quantization, pruning, knowledge
distillation for Raspberry Pi/mobile GPUs. & Lightweight, fast models
for on-device preliminary diagnosis. \\
\textbf{7. System Integration \& Pilot} & API development (HL7/FHIR),
secure communication, dashboard, internal testing. & Functional
HeartLine prototype ready for real-world pilot (simulated initially). \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

\textbf{Source :} \textbf{Adapted from:} Sheller et al. (2020).
\emph{Sci Rep, 10}, 12598.

Simulation across 10 virtual hospitals mimics Algeria's real-world
constraints and tests communication, privacy, and robustness.

\emph{\textbf{\uline{Simulation Setup for Federated Training}:}}
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}23{]}}}

For initial development, the federated training process is simulated
across 10 virtual nodes, each representing a distinct healthcare
institution (e.g., clinics, hospitals). This controlled environment
allows for:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  Easier debugging and performance monitoring.
  \end{quote}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  Scalability testing.
  \end{quote}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  Validation of privacy mechanisms (DP, HE).
  \end{quote}
\item
  \begin{quote}
  Simulation of resource management (communication, computation).
  \end{quote}
\end{itemize}

This simulation provides invaluable insights into the feasibility and
performance of HeartLine\textquotesingle s FL architecture, preparing it
for real-world deployment in the challenging Algerian healthcare
landscape.

\hypertarget{ethics-equity-and-societal-impact}{%
\subsubsection{1.3.4 Ethics, Equity, and Societal
Impact}\label{ethics-equity-and-societal-impact}}

The HeartLine project is designed with a profound awareness of its
\textbf{ethical, legal, and societal implications}, particularly within
the unique context of Algerian healthcare. Our commitment extends beyond
technical performance to ensuring the solution is responsible,
equitable, and beneficial to all stakeholders.

\textbf{a) Privacy-by-Design}

At the forefront is patient data privacy. HeartLine\textquotesingle s
reliance on Federated Learning (FL) directly addresses this by ensuring
raw, identifiable patient ECG data never leaves local premises. This
significantly mitigates risks associated with centralized data storage.
The integration of homomorphic encryption and differential privacy
provides strong, provable guarantees against inference attacks on
aggregated model updates. This rigorously aligns with
Algeria\textquotesingle s Decree No. 22-187 (2022) on Personal Data
Protection, mirroring international frameworks like GDPR. Our data
governance framework includes strict access controls, regular security
audits, and anonymization protocols to prevent re-identification.

\textbf{Table 19: HeartLine\textquotesingle s Privacy and Security
Mechanisms}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.2073}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3799}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.4128}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Mechanism}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Description}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Alignment with Principles/Regulations}
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\textbf{Federated Learning (FL)} & Model training on decentralized local
data; raw patient data remains at the source. & Privacy-by-design,
minimizes data exposure. Crucial for \textbf{Algerian Decree No.
22-187}. \\
\textbf{Homomorphic Encryption (HE)} & Allows computations on encrypted
model updates; central server never sees unencrypted values. & Strong
provable guarantee against data leakage, enhances confidentiality. \\
\textbf{Differential Privacy (DP)} & Adds controlled noise to model
updates, obscuring individual data contributions. & Quantifies and
limits privacy loss, protects individual privacy without compromising
utility. \\
\textbf{Access Controls \& Audits} & Strict controls on who can access
data, regular security checks. & Ensures data integrity and prevents
unauthorized access. \\
\textbf{Anonymization Protocols} & Techniques to remove or obscure
identifying patient information. & Prevents re-identification of
patients, aligns with data protection laws. \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

\textbf{Source :} \textbf{Adapted from:} Truex, S., Yu, F. R., \& Yang,
Y. (2019). Federated learning with privacy: A survey. \emph{ACM
Computing Surveys, 52}(6), 1--33.

This table clearly details how HeartLine\textquotesingle s architectural
choices and technical implementations directly address data privacy and
security concerns. The explicit alignment with
\textbf{Algeria\textquotesingle s Decree No. 22-187 (2022)} underscores
the project\textquotesingle s commitment to local legal compliance,
which is vital for trust and adoption in the Algerian healthcare system.

