\hypertarget{reproducibility-transparency-in-diagnostic-ai}{%
\subsubsection{1.3.5 Reproducibility \& Transparency in Diagnostic
AI}\label{reproducibility-transparency-in-diagnostic-ai}}

HeartLine embraces the principles of reproducibility and transparency as
foundational pillars of ethical AI research, particularly within the
context of sensitive medical diagnostics. This section outlines the
mechanisms, tools, and standards employed to ensure that all
experimental results, model performances, and deployment processes are
verifiable, repeatable, and openly documented.

\textbf{a) Reproducibility Protocols}

\textbf{Table 23: Core Reproducibility Protocols in HeartLine}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.1584}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.4866}}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3550}}@{}}
\toprule()
\begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Component}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Strategy}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\textbf{Outcome}
\end{minipage} \\
\midrule()
\endhead
\textbf{Codebase} & Version-controlled (GitHub, GitLab), modular
structure & Facilitates re-use and traceability \\
\textbf{Datasets} & Publicly cited with exact version/date, local data
shared under NDA & Reproducible data access and ethical governance \\
\textbf{Experiment Logs} & Jupyter notebooks with timestamped runs,
logging seed values & Deterministic outputs across runs \\
\textbf{Model Checkpoints} & Periodic model snapshotting, saved to
DOI-registered repositories & Enables community validation \\
\textbf{Configuration Files} & YAML/JSON files for training,
preprocessing, FL settings & Declarative, auditable experiment setup \\
\textbf{Hardware Specs} & GPU type, RAM, OS, runtime environment logged
& Ensures environment-level reproducibility \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

\textbf{Source :} Adapted from Pineau et al. (2021); Gundersen \&
Kjensmo (2018); HeartLine Internal Protocols.

This table reflects HeartLine's alignment with FAIR AI principles
(Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, Reusable) and highlights how
reproducibility is integrated into both experimental design and project
documentation \protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}25{]}}}.

\textbf{b) Transparency in Methodology and Results}

Transparency is not just about openness, but about enabling peer
scrutiny and downstream improvement.

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Open Access Publication}: All technical methods, evaluation
  metrics, and results are published under open licenses whenever
  possible.
\item
  \textbf{Model Explainability}: Incorporation of XAI techniques (e.g.,
  Grad-CAM, SHAP) into model pipelines enables clinicians to interpret
  AI outputs.
\item
  \textbf{Error Analysis Reports}: Each evaluation cycle includes
  misclassification reviews categorized by diagnosis type, ECG noise,
  and demographic subgroup.
\item
  \textbf{Bias Audits}: Transparent stratification of performance by
  gender, age, and region to detect and mitigate systemic model bias.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{c) Auditability and External Validation}

HeartLine actively encourages independent auditing and validation by
third parties. This creates a collaborative ecosystem and strengthens
clinical trust.

