\hypertarget{additional-ecg-sets-georgia-ludb-physionet-challenge}{%
\subsubsection{2.1.3 Additional ECG Sets: Georgia, LUDB, PhysioNet
Challenge}\label{additional-ecg-sets-georgia-ludb-physionet-challenge}}

To further enhance model generalizability, we include:

- \textbf{Georgia 12-Lead ECG Dataset}: Diverse clinical ECGs from
American hospitals.

- \textbf{LUDB (Lobachevsky University Database)}: Annotated signals
emphasizing wave segmentation.

- \textbf{PhysioNet Challenge (2020, 2021)}: Multisource datasets with
diverse pathology coverage and clinical realism.

These datasets help improve robustness to inter-patient and
inter-institutional variability.

\hypertarget{dataset-curation-and-preprocessing-challenges}{%
\subsubsection{2.1.4 Dataset Curation and Preprocessing
Challenges}\label{dataset-curation-and-preprocessing-challenges}}

Preparing multi-institutional ECG data for federated and centralized
training poses significant challenges:
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}27{]}}}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{Format Standardization}: Conversion of WFDB, CSV, and XML ECG
  formats into unified NumPy arrays.
\item
  \textbf{Label Harmonization}: Mapping heterogeneous label schemes to a
  unified taxonomy.
\item
  \textbf{Ethical Curation}: Anonymization and regulatory compliance
  with Decree 22-187 (Algeria) and GDPR.
\end{itemize}

