This figure visualizes the full data pipeline of a ResNet34-based ECG
diagnosis system. It highlights how 12-lead signals flow through stacked
residual blocks with increasing feature complexity. The architecture is
optimized for temporal signal analysis using 1D convolutions. Global
pooling and dense layers finalize classification across multiple cardiac
conditions. This layout clarifies the model's interpretability and
clinical scalability \protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}30{]}}}.

The next figure illustrates how the ResNet model progressively extracts
features from ECG signals across its layers. Early layers detect basic
waveform structures, while deeper layers abstract clinically meaningful
patterns. It visually supports the interpretability of learned
representations. Such layer-wise evaluation aids model debugging and
refinement. The figure reinforces how deep networks build complex
diagnostic understanding from raw inputs.

