strategies, potential for seeking additional early-stage funding (e.g.,
grants, angel investment), or strategic operational adjustments to
accelerate revenue collection and manage expenses tightly. This aligns
with the "Year 1 Financial Deficit" highlighted in the SWOT analysis as
a key weakness.

\hypertarget{roi-risk-mitigation-and-exit-plan}{%
\subsubsection{4.3.4 ROI, Risk Mitigation and Exit
Plan}\label{roi-risk-mitigation-and-exit-plan}}

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{ROI Potential}: Optimistic breakeven in Year 2, profitability
  by Year 3.
\item
  \textbf{Risk Mitigation}: Cloud spend caps, churn tracking, phased
  hiring.
\item
  \textbf{Exit Options}: Acquisition by medtech firm (GE, Philips),
  health VC exit, or MENA IPO via NESDA
  \protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}58{]}}}.
\end{itemize}

