\hypertarget{testing-performance-and-clinical-validation}{%
\subsection{5.2 Testing, Performance, and Clinical
Validation}\label{testing-performance-and-clinical-validation}}

HeartLine\textquotesingle s development process prioritized rigorous
testing, performance benchmarking, and clinical validation to ensure
that the platform meets the highest standards of accuracy, usability,
and scalability. Each layer of testing was designed to validate the
prototype's reliability and operational readiness in real-world
conditions.

\hypertarget{simulation-testing-protocols}{%
\subsubsection{5.2.1 Simulation Testing
Protocols}\label{simulation-testing-protocols}}

To simulate realistic deployment conditions, HeartLine utilized
federated simulation frameworks reflecting hospital data privacy
constraints. The simulation used the following algorithm:
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}62{]}}}

def federated\_gnn\_training(clinic\_data, num\_rounds=100):

global\_model = initialize\_gnn()

for round in range(num\_rounds):

client\_weights = {[}{]}

for client in clinic\_data:

local\_model = clone(global\_model)

local\_data = preprocess(clinic\_data{[}client{]})

local\_data = augment(local\_data,
method=\textquotesingle hybrid\textquotesingle)

local\_model.fit(local\_data, epochs=10)

client\_weights.append(local\_model.get\_weights())

global\_weights = fed\_avg\_aggregate(client\_weights)

global\_model.set\_weights(global\_weights)

return global\_model

def preprocess(ecg\_data):

signal = bandpass\_filter(ecg\_data, low=0.5, high=40)

signal = normalize(signal)

features = extract\_rr\_intervals(signal)

return features

def predict(ecg\_signal, model):

features = preprocess(ecg\_signal)

graph = build\_graph(features)

prediction = model.predict(graph)

return decode\_prediction(prediction)

This pseudocode represents the data-local training and global model
updating mechanism underlying HeartLine's federated learning system.

Additionally, unit tests were conducted on preprocessing functions such
as filtering and RR extraction, ensuring robustness in signal quality
assessment. Integration testing validated frontend-backend communication
via frameworks like Postman and Jest, simulating diverse clinic
environments. Load testing pushed the system to 1,000 concurrent ECGs to
test speed and fault tolerance.

\hypertarget{performance-metrics-and-benchmarking}{%
\subsubsection{5.2.2 Performance Metrics and
Benchmarking}\label{performance-metrics-and-benchmarking}}

HeartLine established key performance metrics to quantify diagnostic
quality and platform responsiveness:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Latency:} \textless{} 1 second from ECG upload to diagnostic
  feedback.
\item
  \textbf{Accuracy:} \textgreater{} 95\% accuracy in arrhythmia
  classification, benchmarked against validated datasets of over 10,000
  annotated ECGs.
\item
  \textbf{Concurrent Processing:} Platform tested with 1,000
  simultaneous ECG analyses with no drop in speed or accuracy.
\item
  \textbf{Availability:} 99.8\% uptime reported in simulated deployment
  using AWS CloudWatch logs.
\item
  \textbf{Scalability:} Auto-scaling confirmed via AWS GPU orchestration
  triggered by traffic thresholds.
\end{itemize}

These benchmarks ensure that HeartLine can support time-sensitive
decision-making in real clinical environments and scale across
high-volume hospitals.

\hypertarget{prototype-evaluation-method}{%
\subsubsection{5.2.3 Prototype Evaluation
Method}\label{prototype-evaluation-method}}

A multilayered testing strategy was adopted:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Unit Testing:}

  \begin{itemize}
  \item
    Validated preprocessing modules for signal filtering and RR interval
    extraction.
  \item
    Confirmed correct implementation of hybrid augmentation techniques.
  \item
    Ensured that inference pipeline logic produced reliable,
    reproducible results.
  \end{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Integration Testing:}

  \begin{itemize}
  \item
    Verified compatibility between frontend (React 18) and backend
    (Python 3.9 APIs).
  \item
    Confirmed data retrieval/storage performance via PostgreSQL and S3.
  \item
    Assessed API-level interactions with third-party services
    \protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}63{]}}}.
  \end{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Clinical Testing:}

  \begin{itemize}
  \item
    Deployed in 15 pilot clinics across Algeria.
  \item
    Cardiologists reviewed 500 ECGs, evaluating interpretability and
    trust.
  \item
    Usability testing with a Likert scale showed high ratings for
    navigation and output clarity.
  \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

\hypertarget{clinical-use-cases-live-demos}{%
\subsubsection{5.2.4 Clinical Use Cases (Live
Demos)}\label{clinical-use-cases-live-demos}}

HeartLine was demonstrated in live clinical settings to validate
end-to-end functionality:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Routine ECG Screening:} Used as a second opinion tool to
  confirm physician assessments.
\item
  \textbf{Emergency Triage:} Enabled rapid analysis (\textless1s) for
  chest pain presentations.
\item
  \textbf{Post-Operative Monitoring:} Helped clinicians track cardiac
  recovery trends after surgery.
\end{itemize}

Clinicians uploaded ECGs in .hea, .dat, or .csv formats, received
instant federated AI-based analysis, visual explanations, and exported
PDF diagnostic reports. Feedback from these live trials directly
informed further iterations
\protect\hyperlink{references}{\textbf{{[}64{]}}}.

\hypertarget{feedback-and-tuning-iterations}{%
\subsubsection{5.2.5 Feedback and Tuning
Iterations}\label{feedback-and-tuning-iterations}}

Clinical feedback from the 15-site pilot directly informed five
iterative Agile updates:

\begin{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Round 1:} UI redesign for improved diagnostic annotation
  visibility.
\item
  \textbf{Round 2:} Adjustment of arrhythmia detection thresholds to
  reduce false positives.
\item
  \textbf{Round 3:} Added tooltips and explanations for AI outputs to
  improve interpretability.
\item
  \textbf{Round 4:} Mobile layout optimized for tablets and phones.
\item
  \textbf{Round 5:} Introduced an analytics dashboard for clinic
  administrators to track usage and outcomes.
\end{itemize}

These iterations enhanced clinical trust in the system and improved
overall diagnostic transparency. HeartLine is now equipped for
regional-scale deployment with embedded update mechanisms.

\textbf{Source:} Data triangulated from GitHub commit logs, clinic pilot
feedback reports, and AWS CloudWatch logs (2025).

